<template name="window_shell_bg">
<head>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="window_shell_bg.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- Legacy theme's background-only window shell -- a sibling of window_shell.rml (see its own
     comment for the general family) with no header/title-banner sprite swap at all. This variant
     exists specifically for background-context companion documents (the *_bg.rml pattern, see
     npc_shop_bg.rml for the mechanism) -- those are deliberately 100% static markup (no
     RmlModelBinder), and this consumer's real header (when it has one) lives in a separate,
     paired foreground document instead. CGenericConfirmDialog's own generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rml
     is the first consumer.

     No content slot -- unlike the modern fork, legacy's bg document has no separate content-fill
     piece of its own (the sprite-back art already reads as the recessed surface, no extra
     CSS-decorated fill needed), so there is nothing to ever splice in here.

     A consumer links this file as a template resource in its own head section and sets this
     template's name as its own body element's template attribute (see
     generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rml for the worked example), with no children of its own needed.
     As with window_shell.rml, avoid a literal tag-shaped example anywhere in this file's own
     comments, and never join the words head and body with a bare slash, anywhere in this file,
     comments included (RmlUi's Template::Load()/FindTag() text search is comment-blind). -->
<body id="panel">
	<div class="window-shell-sprite-back"></div>
	<div class="window-shell-sprite-top"></div>
	<div class="window-shell-sprite-middle"></div>
	<div class="window-shell-sprite-bottom"></div>
</body>
</template>
